  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186133895,
      "id": "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b",
      "title": "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nI. $F(x,y)=⟨5 y e^{x},\\,x - 5 e^{x}⟩$\n\nII. $F(x,y)=⟨6 y,\\,x⟩$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{2x}{3}+1⟩$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=5 e^{x}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1 - 5 e^{x},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\left(1 - 5 e^{x}\\right)-\\left(5 e^{x}\\right)=\\left(1\\right)+\\left(- 5 e^{x}\\right)-\\left(5 e^{x}\\right)=1 - 10 e^{x}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does *not* give the required area. Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=6$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\left(1\\right)-\\left(6\\right)=\\left(1\\right)-\\left(6\\right)=-5\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{3}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{2}{3},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)-\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{3}\\right)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0d874028-6365-5246-a503-2f1d85258aa3",
